---
import { localizePath, type Locale } from '../../../i18n';
import { site } from '../../../config/site';

const { company, email } = site;

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
---

<section aria-labelledby="who">
  <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Echo is provided by {company.name}, {company.address}, {company.country} ("we"). By installing or using Echo you agree to
    these terms. Nothing in them limits rights you have as a consumer under the law of your country.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="licence">
  <h2 id="licence">2. Your licence</h2>
  <p>
    We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use Echo on devices you own or control. You may
    not resell the app, or copy, modify or reverse-engineer it except where the law allows. Open-source components keep
    their own licences, listed on the <a href={localizePath('/licenses', locale)}>open-source licenses</a> page.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="free-pro">
  <h2 id="free-pro">3. Free and Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Echo is free to download. The free version transcribes the first two minutes of each note. Echo Pro removes that
    limit and unlocks the features described in the app, as a monthly or yearly subscription or a one-time lifetime
    purchase.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Pro is bought, billed and refunded through Google Play under Google Play's terms.</li>
    <li>
      Subscriptions renew automatically until you cancel them in Google Play. Cancelling stops the next renewal; you
      keep Pro until the end of the period you paid for.
    </li>
    <li>
      Lifetime means for as long as we offer Echo, on any device signed in to the same Google account.
    </li>
    <li>
      Pro is digital content delivered right away. In the EU you normally have 14 days to withdraw from an online
      purchase, but for digital content that right ends once delivery starts, if you agreed to that when you paid.
      Google Play asks for that agreement at checkout. Google Play's refund policy applies either way.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="content">
  <h2 id="content">4. Your recordings</h2>
  <p>
    Your recordings and notes belong to you and stay on your device. You are responsible for having the right to
    record. Many countries require the consent of everyone being recorded, so tell people when you record them.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="accuracy">
  <h2 id="accuracy">5. Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Transcripts, speaker labels, summaries and tasks are produced automatically and can contain mistakes. Check them
    before you rely on them, especially for medical, legal, financial or safety matters. Reminders depend on your
    phone's notification and alarm settings.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="liability">
  <h2 id="liability">6. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are liable without limit for intent and gross negligence, and for injury to life, body or health. Otherwise we
    are liable only for breaches of essential obligations, limited to the damage typical and foreseeable for this
    kind of app. Keep backups of notes that matter to you; we cannot recover data stored only on your phone.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="changes">
  <h2 id="changes">7. Changes and ending</h2>
  <p>
    We may update Echo and these terms. If a change affects you materially, we announce it in the app before it takes
    effect. You can stop using Echo at any time by uninstalling it; cancel any subscription in Google Play.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="law">
  <h2 id="law">8. Law and contact</h2>
  <p>
    Slovenian law applies, without taking away the protection of mandatory consumer law in your country of residence.
    Questions: <a href={`mailto:${email.hello}`}>{email.hello}</a>.
  </p>
</section>
